.TH qsh-service 1  "service 0.5.8" 
.SH NAME
qsh\-service \- Manage this machine\*(Aqs platform service unit for its inferred run mode (`docs/CLI.md` §6.18): `install`/`uninstall`/`status` against launchd (macOS) or systemd (Linux) user units. `UNSUPPORTED` on every other platform
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBqsh service\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-jsonl\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-ssh\fR] [\fB\-\-install\-remote\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-install\-remote\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage this machine\*(Aqs platform service unit for its inferred run mode (`docs/CLI.md` §6.18): `install`/`uninstall`/`status` against launchd (macOS) or systemd (Linux) user units. `UNSUPPORTED` on every other platform
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit a single `qsh.cli/v1` JSON envelope on stdout instead of human\-readable text
.TP
\fB\-\-jsonl\fR
Emit newline\-delimited JSON on stdout (reserved for streaming commands; non\-streaming commands emit a single line, same as `\-\-json`)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Increase diagnostic verbosity on stderr (`\-v` info, `\-vv` debug, `\-vvv` trace). Never affects stdout (`docs/CLI.md` §2.2)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress diagnostic output on stderr
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-ssh\fR
Never run ssh on this command\*(Aqs behalf: no automatic bootstrap of an unknown name, and no restarting of a pinned host\*(Aqs serve over ssh when the connection fails (`docs/CLI.md` §7). `qsh pair ssh` is not affected; it is ssh by definition
.TP
\fB\-\-install\-remote\fR
When the ssh bootstrap finds no `qsh` on the remote host (or one too old to answer it), install this machine\*(Aqs release into `~/.local/bin` there without asking (`docs/CLI.md` §7). Works with `\-\-json`
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-install\-remote\fR
Never install or upgrade `qsh` on the remote host, and do not ask; a missing `qsh` ends as `remote_qsh_missing`
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
qsh\-service\-install(1)
Write (or rewrite) the unit for this machine\*(Aqs inferred run mode, create its parent directories, and load and start it through the service manager (ADR\-0051 decision 11). A unit that is already running is not restarted. `\-\-no\-activate` writes the file only
.TP
qsh\-service\-uninstall(1)
Remove the unit for this machine\*(Aqs inferred run mode, if any. Without `\-\-deactivate` a running unit stays running
.TP
qsh\-service\-status(1)
Report whether the unit for this machine\*(Aqs inferred run mode exists. Presence only unless `\-\-live` is given
.SH VERSION
v0.5.8
